This project depends on the following third-party software. Their licenses
differ from maktoob's and continue to apply to their respective code.

  whatsmeow              MPL-2.0     https://github.com/tulir/whatsmeow
    Go library for the WhatsApp multi-device protocol. Linked as a Go module.
    MPL-2.0 is a file-level copyleft licence: modifications to whatsmeow's own
    source files must be shared under MPL-2.0, while maktoob's own source
    remains under MIT.

  whisper.cpp            MIT         https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp
    Speech recognition inference. Invoked as an external process
    (whisper-server), not linked.

  modernc.org/sqlite     BSD-3-Clause  https://gitlab.com/cznic/sqlite
    Pure-Go SQLite driver, including FTS5. Linked as a Go module.

  google.golang.org/protobuf
                         BSD-3-Clause  https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf-go
    Protocol Buffers runtime. Linked as a Go module. Used directly to build
    WhatsApp message fields and to zero whatsmeow's history-sync limits.

  qrterminal            MIT           https://github.com/mdp/qrterminal
    Renders the device-pairing QR code in the terminal. Linked as a Go module.

  rsc.io/qr             BSD-3-Clause  https://github.com/rsc/qr
    QR encoding, pulled in by qrterminal. Linked as a Go module.

  FFmpeg                 LGPL-2.1+ / GPL-2+ depending on build
                                     https://ffmpeg.org
    Audio format conversion. Invoked as an external process, not linked.

  Silero VAD             MIT         https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad
    Voice activity detection model, loaded by whisper.cpp at runtime.

Whisper models (ggml format) are distributed by the whisper.cpp project and
